  "reviewed_source_state": "Source hashes identify the reviewed ownership fix and evidence after the recorded base revision. 2026-11-23 review (PR #2898): crates/gateway/src/routes/mod.rs adds a private `mod tasks_opening;` (no #[path]; resolves to src/routes/tasks_opening.rs, which imports no transport, EST, generation or source-lifetime item) and mounts POST /api/v1/tasks/intent-opening inside the existing router chain, so it inherits the same layers, state and listeners. No listener, bind, EST route, admission, generation, epoch or deadline check changed, so the source-owned lifetime boundary the model covers is unaffected; reviewed_blob moves to the current bytes and base_blob stays the recorded base. 2026-11-23: re-pinned after behaviour-preserving lint and format repairs: cargo fmt of files main left unformatted; spiffe-source source.rs drops a test-only import; WaitError boxes its SourceStatus (clippy result_large_err; same variants and observations); xkeys open drops a redundant nonce re-conversion; est_freshness.rs is loaded once. No modeled transition, guard or persistence changed. Lean suites not run here (no Lean toolchain); Rust regressions for spiffe-source, transport-security, gateway routes/transport and xkeys passed, and every check-drift.py matches. 2026-11-23 merge review (main 760292b7 into #2900): crates/gateway/src/routes/mod.rs is the union of two disjoint reviewed hunks, main's private tasks_opening module and POST /api/v1/tasks/intent-opening route (PR #2898) and this branch's test-only est_freshness alias to est_wire::freshness; no listener, bind, layer, admission or other route changed, so the digest is recomputed for the merged bytes. Regression runs on the merged tree are recorded in the follow-up note. 2026-11-23 review (CodeQL rust/unsafe-deserialization fixes, branch claude/rust-deserialization): crates/gateway/src/lib.rs changes only two test-only pact_coverage source-order oracles (sync_blobs now names `wire::opaque_push_body(body)` after `require_session`; the GitHub webhook order is asserted across github_webhook_delivery.rs, where signature shape, secret, MAC and the typed summary decode now run in that order, and github_webhook.rs, where the verified delivery precedes claim and outbox). crates/gateway/src/transport/bindings.rs adds `PutBody`/`accept_put`, the operator PUT body read through opensesame_host_core::bounded_json (at most MAX_BINDINGS_BYTES, decoded straight into the strict ServiceBindingSet, then `validate()`, with parse_bounded's error shape); parse_bounded, load, load_file, put_cas and every stored/file path are unchanged. crates/host-core/Cargo.toml adds http-body-util (already in the graph; LengthLimitError detection) and futures as a dev-dependency for the new bounded_json module. No listener, bind, layer, admission, generation, epoch, source-history, trust-selection or peer-domain item changed, so the modeled boundary is unaffected; reviewed digests move to the current bytes. Executed: cargo test -p opensesame-gateway --lib (1270 passed, 10 ignored), --features testkit --test testkit (4 passed, 1 ignored), opensesame-host-core (48), opensesame-daemon (321 passed; 1 pre-existing environment failure in runner, untouched); cargo clippy -D warnings on the three crates and cargo fmt --all --check clean. Lean suites not run here (no Lean toolchain). 2026-11-24: verify.sh builds through the formal-cargo freshness session (declared reviewed patch sqlx-sqlite=patches/vendor/sqlx-sqlite-0.9.0), replacing the plain-cargo fallback recorded in e1142ec99; the reviewed vendored-SQLx verifier (blob 1d9776a6, the bytes the SPIFFE suite pins) is added to the covered sources and executed by check-drift.py on every input check. No covered implementation source changed.",
